        "\n",
        "## Practicing with Tables\n",
        "\n",
        "We're going to look at a dataset in R called `starwars`. It includes data about Star Wars characters.\n",
        "\n",
        "Make a table of the number of characters with each hair color using the variable `hair_color`.\n",
        "\n",
        "```{code-blanks}\n",
        "#| blank:\n",
        "#|   target: starwars\n",
        "#|   prefill: false\n",
        "#|   occurrence: 1\n",
        "#|   match: token\n",
        "#| blank:\n",
        "#|   target: hair_color\n",
        "#|   prefill: false\n",
        "#|   occurrence: 1\n",
        "#|   match: token\n",
        "\n",
        "count(starwars, hair_color)\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "The other variables in the dataset that we can look at this way are `homeworld`, `species`, `eye_color`, `skin_color`, `sex`, and `gender`. Choose one of them to make a table.\n",
        "\n",
        "```{code-blanks}\n",
        "#| blank:\n",
        "#|   target: starwars\n",
        "#|   prefill: false\n",
        "#|   occurrence: 1\n",
        "#|   match: token\n",
        "#| blank:\n",
        "#|   target: \"blank1\"\n",
        "#|   prefill: false\n",
        "#|   occurrence: 1\n",
        "#|   match: token\n",
        "\n",
        "count(starwars, \"blank1\")\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "Now choose any two of those categorical variables to make a table showing characters split by both of those variables. \n",
        "\n",
        "```{code-blanks}\n",
        "#| blank:\n",
        "#|   target: starwars\n",
        "#|   prefill: false\n",
        "#|   occurrence: 1\n",
        "#|   match: token\n",
        "#| blank:\n",
        "#|    target: \"blank1\"\n",
        "#|    prefill: false\n",
        "#|    occurrence: 1\n",
        "#|    match: token\n",
        "#| blank:\n",
        "#|    target: \"blank2\"\n",
        "#|    prefill: false\n",
        "#|    occurrence: 1\n",
        "#|    match: token\n",
        "\n",
        "count(starwars, \"blank1\", \"blank2\")\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "Take a screenshot of this table. This will be part of your submission for this assignment, so either save it or put it in a document.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Practicing with Graphs\n",
        "\n",
        "Make a bar graph of characters' hair colors with appropriate labels.\n",
        "\n",
        "```{code-blanks}\n",
        "#| blank:\n",
        "#|   target: starwars\n",
        "#|   prefill: false\n",
        "#|   occurrence: 1\n",
        "#|   match: token\n",
        "#| blank:\n",
        "#|   target: hair_color\n",
        "#|   prefill: false\n",
        "#|   occurrence: 1\n",
        "#|   match: token\n",
        "#| blank:\n",
        "#|   target: blank1\n",
        "#|   prefill: false\n",
        "#|   occurrence: 1\n",
        "#|   match: token\n",
        "#| blank:\n",
        "#|   target: blank2\n",
        "#|   prefill: false\n",
        "#|   occurrence: 1\n",
        "#|   match: token\n",
        "#| blank:\n",
        "#|   target: blank3\n",
        "#|   prefill: false\n",
        "#|   occurrence: 1\n",
        "#|   match: token\n",
        "\n",
        "ggplot(starwars) +\n",
        "  aes(x = hair_color) +\n",
        "  geom_bar() +\n",
        "  labs(\n",
        "    title = \"blank1\",\n",
        "    x = \"blank2\",\n",
        "    y = \"blank3\"\n",
        "  )\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "Make a bar graph in the style of your choice using two of the categorical variables. Again, include appropriate lables\n",
        "\n",
